Usage: xnvme driver-attach <bdf>... [--driver <name>] [--force] [--all]
                           [--dry-run]

Move each named NVMe controller function off the kernel nvme driver,
onto the platform's userspace driver unless --driver names another:
on Linux vfio-pci when the host has IOMMU groups or vfio no-IOMMU mode,
else uio_pci_generic, and nic_uio on FreeBSD.
A function whose namespaces are in use is refused; --force overrides
only the refusal of a namespace carrying a filesystem or partition table.
--all attaches every function on the kernel nvme driver,
and skips those in use.
